Set up Perl::Critic profile that makes Langertha's coding conventions machine-checkable, then enforce it via Dist::Zilla so it runs on every dzil test.

## Goal
Adopt a Perl::Critic profile that makes Langertha's coding conventions machine-checkable, then enforce it via Dist::Zilla so it runs on every dzil test.

## Scope (approved by maintainer)
- Baseline: naming policies from open PR lmist:readiness/naming-consistency (NamingConventions::Capitalization + NamingConventions::ProhibitAmbiguousNames)
- Extend with always-on, low-noise policies that pass CLEAN on current tree (each verified individually):
  - CodeLayout::ProhibitTrailingWhitespace
  - CodeLayout::RequireConsistentNewlineAtEndOfFile
  - ValuesAndExpressions::ProhibitStringyEval
  - ControlStructures::ProhibitPostfixControls
  - Subroutines::ProhibitExplicitReturnUndef
  - Subroutines::RequireFinalReturn
  - TestingAndDebugging::RequireUseStrict
  - TestingAndDebugging::RequireUseWarnings
- Exemptions: vLLM brand capitalization, Moose lifecycle (BUILD/FOREIGNBUILDARGS/DEMOLISH/...), $VERSION, %ROLE_TO_CAPS

## Files
- .perlcriticrc (NEW)
- dist.ini — add Dist::Zilla::Plugin::Test::Perl::Critic = 0
- cpanfile — test prereqs for Perl::Critic
- lib/Langertha/Role/OpenAPI.pm — rename $operationId/$opId to $operation_id/$op_id
- README.md — Coding conventions section
- CLAUDE.md — naming bullet
- Changes — changelog entry
- xt/release/perl-critic.t — generated by dzil plugin

## Out of scope
- The open PR (lmist:readiness/naming-consistency) — leave untouched
- .github/workflows CI — not in scope without explicit ask
- dzil release — forbidden without go-ahead

